From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:38:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sdm845: keep an optional codec MCLK enabled

The comma 3X speaker and microphones go through a MAX98089 codec that
runs from the RPMh LN_BB_CLK2 19.2 MHz clock. openpilot programs the
MAX98089 itself over i2c-dev, read-modify-writing its registers from a
fixed table, so it has no kernel driver and nothing enables its master
clock: without it the codec PLLs have no reference and there is no
sound.

Let the sound card take an optional "mclk" clock and hold it enabled
for as long as the card is bound, which covers every stream on both
MI2S links.

This is not intended for upstream. There the MAX98089 would be described
with the existing max98088 driver as the codec of both links, owning its
MCLK. That needs openpilot to configure the codec through ALSA controls
instead of raw register writes, and the driver to learn the digital
microphone and DAI port selection from DT, which today come only from
platform data or are hard-coded the other way round.

Based on Trey Moen's vamOS PR 128.

[adeeb: split from the tertiary MI2S change, write the commit message]
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sdm845.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sdm845.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sdm845.c
index 3cc53cd4eb..4a5cbcd799 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sdm845.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sdm845.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6afe.h>
+#include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <sound/core.h>
@@ -576,6 +577,7 @@ static int sdm845_snd_platform_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct snd_soc_card *card;
 	struct sdm845_snd_data *data;
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
+	struct clk *mclk;
 	int ret;
 
 	card = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*card), GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -587,6 +589,10 @@ static int sdm845_snd_platform_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (!data)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	mclk = devm_clk_get_optional_enabled(dev, "mclk");
+	if (IS_ERR(mclk))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(mclk), "failed to enable mclk\n");
+
 	card->driver_name = DRIVER_NAME;
 	card->dapm_widgets = sdm845_snd_widgets;
 	card->num_dapm_widgets = ARRAY_SIZE(sdm845_snd_widgets);
